    "source_text": "# KO-reset snowball under flat Black-Scholes.\n#\n# The hard part of this payoff is a REGIME SWITCH. The trade runs a pre-KI KO\n# schedule (barrier 103) to maturity_pre; only once it knocks in at 80 does it\n# switch to a second, lower KO schedule (barrier 95) running on to\n# maturity_post. Two value surfaces therefore live on different horizons -- and\n# that is precisely what both deterministic engines got wrong before audit #13,\n# maturing the not-yet-knocked-in surface on the post-KI schedule.\n#\n# Environment, economic scale and bounds are identical to snowball_flat_bsm and\n# phoenix_flat_bsm on purpose: at multiplier 200, inception spot 100 and\n# notional 20,000 the delta quantum and the reference move are both exactly\n# 1.0, so a raw error IS a contract error and all three studies share one axis.\n#\n# Bound calibration (release procedure section 7, step 4). The cell gate needs\n# the benchmark standard error inside 0.25 x 0.5 = 0.125 c. Measured at this\n# budget (4 batches x 65,536 paths, paired bumps): pv 0.0110, delta 0.0087,\n# gamma 0.0297. Gamma is the binding quantity at a 4.2x margin -- tighter than\n# the other two studies, this being a longer-dated two-regime payoff -- but\n# still compatible, and the sampler may take up to 32 batches to sharpen it.\n#\n# Offline study (minutes, not seconds). Run it with:\n#   python -m quantark.modelvalidation run example/modelvalidation/ko_reset_flat_bsm.yaml\n# Add --quick for a wiring check that is explicitly not bankable evidence.\n\nstudy: ko-reset-flat-bsm\nschema: 1\n\nquantities: [pv, delta, gamma]\n\nbounds:\n  cell: 0.5\n  mean_signed_bias: 0.1\n\nsampling:\n  paths_per_batch: 65536\n  min_batches: 4\n  max_batches: 32\n  seed: 20260818\n  bump: 0.01\n\neconomic_scale:\n  builder: hedge_contracts\n  params:\n    hedge_multiplier: 200.0\n    hedge_inception_spot: 100.0\n    notional: 20000.0\n\nenvironment:\n  builder: flat_bsm\n  params:\n    spot: 100.0\n    vol: 0.22\n    rate: 0.025\n    div_yield: 0.03\n\nproduct:\n  builder: equity.ko_reset_snowball\n  params:\n    initial_price: 100.0\n    strike: 100.0\n    maturity_pre: 1.0\n    maturity_post: 2.0\n    pre_ko_barrier: 103.0\n    pre_ko_rate: 0.15\n    post_ko_barrier: 95.0\n    post_ko_rate: 0.03\n    ki_barrier: 80.0\n    ki_continuous: true\n    contract_multiplier: 1.0\n\nreference:\n  builder: equity.ko_reset_snowball.mc_rqmc\n  params: {}\n\ncandidates:\n  - builder: equity.ko_reset_snowball.pde\n    params: {accuracy: standard}\n  - builder: equity.ko_reset_snowball.quad\n    params: {grid_points: 1001}\n\ncases:\n  # At inception, clear of both KO barriers and well above KI.\n  - {name: ordinary}\n  # Just under the pre-KI KO barrier: the KO discontinuity sits inside the bump\n  # stencil, where deterministic gamma usually breaks first.\n  - {name: near_pre_ko, environment: {spot: 102.5}}\n  # Just above the KI barrier: the regime switch is one small move away, so both\n  # surfaces and the transition between them are in play at once.\n  - {name: near_ki, environment: {spot: 80.5}}\n  # Below the KI barrier: already knocked in at valuation, which exercises the\n  # post-KI schedule and its lower KO barrier directly rather than through the\n  # transition.\n  - {name: below_ki, environment: {spot: 76.0}}\n  # Low vol: the KI barrier is rarely reached, so almost all the value sits on\n  # the pre-KI surface and its maturity must be exactly right.\n  - {name: low_vol, environment: {vol: 0.12}}\n  # Short horizons on both legs: few observations left and time discretization\n  # error has nowhere to average out.\n  - {name: near_expiry, product: {maturity_pre: 0.25, maturity_post: 0.5}}\n  # Discrete KI monitoring instead of continuous. This is a different code path\n  # in every engine -- the continuous one runs a Brownian-bridge correction that\n  # the discrete one never touches -- so it is certified explicitly.\n  - {name: discrete_ki, product: {ki_continuous: false}}\n"
  },
